    level: "intermediate",
    title: "ALLERGIC REACTIONS TO COSMETICS",
    text: "Cosmetics are among the most common causes of allergic skin reactions. The wide variety of chemicals used in perfumes, hair dyes, and skin creams means that almost anyone can develop a sensitivity to one or more ingredients. Symptoms range from mild redness and itching to severe swelling and blistering. Paradoxically, products marketed as hypoallergenic or natural are not always safer, as even natural ingredients such as plant extracts can trigger reactions in sensitive individuals. Dermatologists recommend patch testing any new product before applying it widely, and carefully reading ingredient lists, particularly for those with a history of allergies.",
    translation_uz: "Kosmetika mahsulotlari teri allergik reaktsiyalarining eng keng tarqalgan sabablaridan biri hisoblanadi. Atirlar, soch bo'yoqlari va teri kremlarida ishlatiladigan kimyoviy moddalarning xilma-xilligi deyarli har bir kishi bir yoki bir nechta ingredientga sezgirlik rivojlantirishi mumkinligini anglatadi. Belgilar engil qizarish va qichishishdan tortib og'ir shishish va pufakchalargacha bo'lishi mumkin. Paradoksal tarzda, gipoallergen yoki tabiiy deb sotilayotgan mahsulotlar har doim ham xavfsiz emas, chunki o'simlik ekstraktlari kabi tabiiy ingredientlar ham sezgir odamlarda reaktsiyani qo'zg'atishi mumkin.",
