    title: "PACIFIC SALMON",
    text: "The salmon industry in the Pacific Northwest of North America has long been one of the region's most valuable economic sectors. Japanese demand for salmon, particularly for use in sushi and sashimi, has driven significant growth in both wild-caught and farmed salmon production. For decades, the Japanese market was considered the premium destination for Pacific salmon, with buyers willing to pay top prices for the freshest fish. However, rising competition from Norwegian and Chilean salmon farms, combined with changing Japanese consumer preferences, has introduced new pressures on Pacific salmon exporters, forcing many to diversify their markets.",
    translation_uz: "Shimoliy Amerikaning Tinch okean shimoli-g'arbidagi qizilbaliq sanoati uzoq vaqtdan beri mintaqaning eng qimmatli iqtisodiy tarmoqlaridan biri bo'lib kelmoqda. Yaponiyaning qizilbaliqqa bo'lgan talabi, ayniqsa sushi va sashimi uchun, ham yovvoyi ovlangan, ham yetishtiriladigan qizilbaliq ishlab chiqarishni sezilarli darajada o'stirdi. O'nlab yillar davomida Yaponiya bozori Tinch okean qizilbaliqlari uchun premium manzil hisoblangan, xaridorlar eng yangi baliqlar uchun yuqori narx to'lashga tayyor. Biroq Norvegiya va Chili qizilbaliq fermalaridan o'sib borayotgan raqobat yangi bosimlar olib keldi.",
