    text: "Art theft is a sophisticated crime that requires meticulous planning, insider knowledge, and often the involvement of an international network of dealers and collectors. Major museum heists rarely result from opportunistic theft; rather, they are carefully orchestrated operations targeting specific works with established black market demand. Stolen masterpieces seldom appear at public auctions — they circulate in the shadowy world of private sales, used as collateral in criminal transactions or stored for decades until authorities lose interest. Recovery rates for stolen art remain surprisingly low, and many experts believe that thousands of stolen works remain hidden in private collections.",
